# Limine boot configuration. limine-update regenerates /boot/limine.conf from
# this file; sync-config-post.sh runs it whenever this file changes.
#
# KERNEL_CMDLINE[default] applies to every generated entry, so the LTS kernel
# inherits it too -- which is what makes booting LTS a usable A/B test.
#
# Everything on the KERNEL_CMDLINE line below is CachyOS's stock installer
# cmdline -- verified against a 22 Aug copy as `quiet nowatchdog splash` plus
# the rw/rootflags/luks/root tokens and nothing else, no mitigations=, no
# zswap, no pstate knob -- except the trailing xe parameter. No package owns
# this file, so this comment is the only record of the stock line.
#
# The crash-capture instrumentation that lived here from 23 to 28 Aug is gone:
# dropping `nowatchdog`/`quiet`/`splash`, `pstore.backend=efi
# efi_pstore.pstore_disable=0`, and the panic sysctls that were in
# /etc/sysctl.d/99-lockup-capture.conf. It ran across six hangs and captured
# nothing, and that null result is itself the finding. The efi pstore backend
# was confirmed registered and the NMI hard-lockup detector confirmed armed,
# yet the detector never fired once -- so the hang stops cores below the
# kernel's reach (hung SMI/SMM handler, PMC fault, or a C-state the silicon
# does not return from). pstore only writes on panic, no panic ever happened,
# so it had nothing to persist. Re-arming it would not add to that.
#
# Panel Replay. Upstream drivers/gpu/drm/i915/display/intel_quirks.c carries a
# quirk_disable_edp_panel_replay entry for PCI subsystem 1028:0dba -- this exact
# machine, the XPS 16 DA16260 -- because the Panel Replay Selective Update
# handshake wedges the display engine on it. The entry is gated on the panel's
# sink IEEE OUI 00:22:b9, which is the Samsung OLED option. This unit has the
# Sharp LQ160N1 (EDID SHP 0x15C4), so the quirk never fires and
# i915_edp_psr_status reports "Panel Replay Selective Update enabled (Early
# Transport)" -- the mode upstream considers broken here.
#
# The published failure for that mode (ASUS B9406CAA, same xe/Panther Lake
# generation, same Early Transport path) is "Timed out waiting PSR idle state"
# plus "DSB 0 timed out waiting for idle", ending with the internal panel black
# and only a reboot recovering it. Our hang starts the same way -- eDP-1 scanout
# corrupting while DP-1 stays clean -- and then takes the whole box with it.
#
# So xe.enable_panel_replay=0 is the only non-stock token here, and the sole
# remaining A/B variable. It replaced a 60Hz pin on both outputs (hyperion.lua
# is back to mode = "preferred"), which was a blunter guess and cost the panel
# half its refresh rate; this one is the fix upstream already wrote for this
# model, just not for this panel. Baseline is ~1 hang/day, so a crash-free week
# clears it. Drop the parameter if the hangs continue -- it is not free, Panel
# Replay is a real idle-power win.
ESP_PATH="/boot"
KERNEL_CMDLINE[default]+="quiet nowatchdog splash rw rootflags=subvol=/@ rd.luks.uuid=e6a763ab-0c7d-4e55-9ac4-d349b234d5a7 root=/dev/mapper/luks-e6a763ab-0c7d-4e55-9ac4-d349b234d5a7 xe.enable_panel_replay=0"
BOOT_ORDER="*, *lts, *fallback, Snapshots"
